sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W as Usage worker
    participant C as Invoice closing API
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over W,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C<br/>Event row: usage_inbox.source = S and usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Catalog advisory (65102, 2): protects price_versions, not a column
    Note over W,D: A valid usage_inbox row already exists for month M.<br/>Month M has ended and is eligible for closing.
    alt Worker gets the account first
        W->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        C->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        Note over C,D: WAIT until worker commit or rollback
        W->>D: Shared catalog lock, FOR UPDATE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Account usage into M, allocate credit, COMMIT
        D-->>C: Account lock granted
        C->>D: Read processed M groups and allocated credit
        C->>D: Publish immutable invoice and closure, COMMIT
        Note over C,D: This usage_inbox row is included in invoice M
    else Closing gets the account first
        C->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        W->>D: BEGIN, FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
        Note over W,D: WAIT, no financial changes yet
        C->>D: Publish only already processed M groups, COMMIT
        D-->>W: Account lock granted
        W->>D: Shared catalog lock, FOR UPDATE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Read the committed closure
        W->>D: Account into an eligible later billing_month, COMMIT
        Note over W,D: Keep original usage_month and historical price.<br/>Invoice M is unchanged.
    end
